§§ `בדיקת הנספחים`

-- The checks: what the agreement, the completion agreement and the base
-- agreement say a cell should be, run over every cell, with the first
-- part's checks (a check names the cell by its printed row and grade, and
-- the agorot the printed cell is off the rule's figure).

-- (1) The conversion tables are the same tables with intermediate grades
-- (the base agreement's §46(א), §71(א), §98(א)): every cell a pay table
-- prints, its conversion table prints at the same row and grade.
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex א'1` `third-part annex א'3`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex א'2` `third-part annex א'4`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex א'8` `third-part annex א'9`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex א'13` `third-part annex א'15`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex א'22` `third-part annex א'23`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex ב'1` `third-part annex ב'2`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex ב'3` `third-part annex ב'4`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex ב'5` `third-part annex ב'6`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex ב'7` `third-part annex ב'8`)

-- (2) The total update. §4(א) sets every table 5.75% above the table in
-- force before 1.1.2011, and the first part set its tables 2.25% above the
-- same table; the corpus does not hold that table, so each cell is set
-- beside the first part's cell at the same row and grade raised by
-- 1.0575/1.0225, rounded to the agora (convention rounding.half). Where both
-- printed cells are that table's cell raised and rounded to the agora, the
-- two can be at most an agora apart at a whole grade (each rounding moves a
-- cell by at most half an agora); an intermediate grade, the mean of its
-- neighbours rounded, may drift one more.
@desc A table of this agreement beside the first part's table it updates.
DECLARE `third-part table beside its first-part table` HAS
    `the third part's table` IS A `salary table`
    `the first part's table` IS A `salary table`

GIVEN new IS A `salary table`, old IS A `salary table`
GIVETH A `third-part table beside its first-part table`
DECIDE `beside` new old IS
    `third-part table beside its first-part table` WITH
        `the third part's table` IS new
        `the first part's table` IS old

`the third part's rise over the first part's tables` MEANS
    (1 PLUS `the total update of the reform tables from 1.4.2013`) DIVIDED BY (1 PLUS `the 2011 table update rate`)

-- The completion agreement's 4% of 1.1.2012, measured the same way.
`the completion agreement's rise over the first part's tables` MEANS
    (1 PLUS `the total update of the reform tables from 1.1.2012`) DIVIDED BY (1 PLUS `the 2011 table update rate`)

GIVEN factor IS A NUMBER, p IS A `third-part table beside its first-part table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cell check`
DECIDE `the cells beside the first part's raised by` factor p IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD
                                      CONSIDER `the cell of` (p's `the first part's table`) (r's `row place`) (c's grade)
                                      WHEN JUST o THEN LIST (`a check of` (r's `row place`) (c's grade) (c's pay) (`to the agora` (o TIMES factor)))
                                      WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY)
                                 (r's `row cells`)))
                (p's `the third part's table`'s `rows`))

GIVEN p IS A `third-part table beside its first-part table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cell address`
DECIDE `the whole-grade cells off the total update in` p IS
    filter (GIVEN a YIELD FLOOR (a's `at grade`) EQUALS a's `at grade`)
           (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the cells beside the first part's raised by` `the third part's rise over the first part's tables` p))

-- Every table the first part also annexed, beside it (the 85% tables
-- א'13, א'15, א'17, א'19, א'21 are new; the first part's deputies' tables
-- were at 75%, and are here א'14, א'16, א'18, א'20).
`א'3 beside א3'` MEANS `beside` `third-part annex א'3` `annex א3'`
`א'6 beside א6'` MEANS `beside` `third-part annex א'6` `annex א6'`
`א'7 beside א7'` MEANS `beside` `third-part annex א'7` `annex א7'`

`the other tables beside the first part's` MEANS
    LIST `beside` `third-part annex א'1` `annex א1'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'2` `annex א2'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'4` `annex א4'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'5` `annex א5'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'8` `annex א8'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'9` `annex א9'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'10` `annex א10'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'11` `annex א11'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'12` `annex א12'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'14` `annex א14'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'16` `annex א15'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'18` `annex א16'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'20` `annex א17'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'22` `annex א18'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'23` `annex א19'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'24` `annex א20'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'25` `annex א21'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'26` `annex א22'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex ב'1` `annex ב1'`, `beside` `third-part annex ב'2` `annex ב2'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex ב'3` `annex ב3'`, `beside` `third-part annex ב'4` `annex ב4'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex ב'5` `annex ב5'`, `beside` `third-part annex ב'6` `annex ב6'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex ב'7` `annex ב7'`, `beside` `third-part annex ב'8` `annex ב8'`

`every table beside the first part's` MEANS
    append (LIST `א'3 beside א3'`, `א'6 beside א6'`, `א'7 beside א7'`) `the other tables beside the first part's`

`all the total-update checks` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN p YIELD `the cells beside the first part's raised by` `the third part's rise over the first part's tables` p)
                `every table beside the first part's`)

-- F-ofek-hadash-tosefet-2011-third-b: three cells of the teachers'
-- conversion tables are two or three agorot below what 5.75% makes of the
-- first part's cell — א'3 at seniority 2, grade 4 (7,315.06); א'6 at
-- seniority 4, grade 2 (4,502.36); א'7 at seniority 33, grade 7
-- (7,801.36) — and each is as far off the steps its own table prints.
-- Every other whole-grade cell of the thirty tables is within an agora;
-- א'6 at seniority 4, grade 4 (5,203.07) is exactly 5.75% of the first
-- part's 5,030.86 (it was off while the corpus misread that cell 5,030.88,
-- MMS-531). The reading adopted: the printed cell governs
-- (convention rounding.printed-figure).
`three conversion cells are two or three agorot below the total update` MEANS
        `the whole-grade cells off the total update in` `א'3 beside א3'` EQUALS LIST (`cell address` 2 4)
    AND `the whole-grade cells off the total update in` `א'6 beside א6'` EQUALS LIST (`cell address` 4 2)
    AND `the whole-grade cells off the total update in` `א'7 beside א7'` EQUALS LIST (`cell address` 33 7)
    AND all (GIVEN p YIELD null (`the whole-grade cells off the total update in` p)) `the other tables beside the first part's`
    AND elem (`cell address` 2 4) (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the rate steps of` `third-part annex א'3`))
    AND elem (`cell address` 4 2) (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the rate steps of` `third-part annex א'6`))
    AND elem (`cell address` 33 7) (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the rate steps of` `third-part annex א'7`))
    AND `to the agora` (5030.86 TIMES `the third part's rise over the first part's tables`) EQUALS 5203.07
    AND `the cell of` `third-part annex א'6` 4 4 EQUALS JUST 5203.07
#ASSERT `three conversion cells are two or three agorot below the total update`

-- How far the whole tables are from the update: 3,911 cells beside the
-- first part's, of which 1,051 are an agora off.
#ASSERT count `all the total-update checks` EQUALS 3911
#ASSERT count (`the misses in` `all the total-update checks`) EQUALS 1051

-- F-ofek-hadash-tosefet-2011-third-a: six annexes print "updated from
-- 1.1.2012" (א'14, א'16, א'18, א'20 — the conversion-only tables at 75%,
-- printed under the labels they carried elsewhere — and א'19 and א'24),
-- while §4(א) attaches the tables updated from 1.4.2013. Their cells are
-- the 1.4.2013 update: the five the first part also annexed are within an
-- agora of 5.75% (above), and none is within an agora of the completion
-- agreement's 4% of 1.1.2012; א'19 is within an agora of 85% of this
-- agreement's own א'11. The reading adopted: the tables apply from
-- 1.4.2013, as §4(א) says (convention reading.misprint).
`the six annexes beside the first part's` MEANS
    LIST `beside` `third-part annex א'14` `annex א14'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'16` `annex א15'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'18` `annex א16'`, `beside` `third-part annex א'20` `annex א17'`,
         `beside` `third-part annex א'24` `annex א20'`

`the six annexes beside the 4% of 1.1.2012` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN p YIELD `the cells beside the first part's raised by` `the completion agreement's rise over the first part's tables` p)
                `the six annexes beside the first part's`)

`six annexes print 1.1.2012 under cells of the 1.4.2013 update` MEANS
        NOT (`the day six annexes print as their update` EQUALS `the third part's tables are updated from`)
    AND `the day most annexes print as their update` EQUALS `the third part's tables are updated from`
    AND count `the annexes printed as updated from 1.1.2012` EQUALS 6
    AND all (GIVEN p YIELD null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the cells beside the first part's raised by` `the third part's rise over the first part's tables` p)))
            `the six annexes beside the first part's`
    AND count (`the cells off by more than` 100 `agorot in` `the six annexes beside the 4% of 1.1.2012`) EQUALS count `the six annexes beside the 4% of 1.1.2012`
    AND count `the six annexes beside the 4% of 1.1.2012` EQUALS 135
    AND null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the 85% share on the update day` `third-part annex א'11` `third-part annex א'19`))
#ASSERT `six annexes print 1.1.2012 under cells of the 1.4.2013 update`

-- (3) The first deputies' tables. The completion agreement's §56 made the
-- first deputy's table 85% of the principal's from 1.3.2011; the tables at
-- 75% (the base agreement's §92(א)) are annexed for the conversion only,
-- as the completion agreement's §63 places an existing deputy first on
-- the 75% table and then in the parallel 85% cell. Each deputy's cell
-- beside the share of the principal's cell at the same row and grade,
-- rounded to the agora (convention rounding.half).
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER, principals IS A `salary table`, deputies IS A `salary table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cell check`
DECIDE `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` share principals deputies IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD
                                      CONSIDER `the cell of` principals (r's `row place`) (c's grade)
                                      WHEN JUST p THEN LIST (`a check of` (r's `row place`) (c's grade) (c's pay)
                                                                (`to the agora` (share TIMES p)))
                                      WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY)
                                 (r's `row cells`)))
                (deputies's `rows`))

`the 85% share on the update day` MEANS
    `the first deputies' share of the principals' table on` `the third part's tables are updated from`

`the 85% tables beside the principals'` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the 85% share on the update day` `third-part annex א'8` `third-part annex א'13`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the 85% share on the update day` `third-part annex א'9` `third-part annex א'15`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the 85% share on the update day` `third-part annex א'10` `third-part annex א'17`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the 85% share on the update day` `third-part annex א'11` `third-part annex א'19`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the 85% share on the update day` `third-part annex א'12` `third-part annex א'21`)

`the 75% tables beside the principals'` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` `third-part annex א'9` `third-part annex א'14`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` `third-part annex א'10` `third-part annex א'16`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` `third-part annex א'11` `third-part annex א'18`,
                 `the deputies' cells beside a share of the principals'` `the first deputies' share of the principals' table` `third-part annex א'12` `third-part annex א'20`)

-- F-ofek-hadash-tosefet-2011-third-c: 31 of the 123 cells of the five 85%
-- tables, and 22 of the 108 cells of the four 75% tables, are an agora off
-- their share of the principals' cell; none more. The reading adopted: the
-- printed cell governs (convention rounding.printed-figure).
`the deputies' tables are not their share of the principals' to the agora` MEANS
        count `the 85% tables beside the principals'` EQUALS 123
    AND count (`the misses in` `the 85% tables beside the principals'`) EQUALS 31
    AND null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` `the 85% tables beside the principals'`)
    AND count `the 75% tables beside the principals'` EQUALS 108
    AND count (`the misses in` `the 75% tables beside the principals'`) EQUALS 22
    AND null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` `the 75% tables beside the principals'`)
#ASSERT `the deputies' tables are not their share of the principals' to the agora`
#ASSERT `the 85% share on the update day` EQUALS 85%

-- The conversion table of a principal in the senior grade ('בכיר', א'10)
-- prints the same cells as the academic deputies' 75% table (א'14), as the
-- first part's א10' and א14' did; no rule asks it, and none forbids it.
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `third-part annex א'10` `third-part annex א'14`)

-- (4) The steps each table prints, the first part's checks run over this
-- agreement's tables: a teachers' row's rise over the row above (2%, then
-- 1%), a header's rise of each grade over the grade before it (7.5%, 8.5%,
-- a principal's 8.75%), a principals' or deputies' level's rise in shekels.
`all the third part's teachers' step checks` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD `the percentage steps of` t) `the third part's teachers' tables`)

GIVEN t IS A `salary table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every level is within half a shekel of its printed shekels` t IF
    null (`the cells off by more than` 49 `agorot in` (`the shekel steps of` t))

-- F-ofek-hadash-tosefet-2011-third-d: the steps the tables print do not
-- make their cells. The percentage steps make a teachers' cell from its
-- printed neighbour only to within an agora or two (1,408 of 5,231 checks
-- miss, the three cells of F-ofek-hadash-tosefet-2011-third-b among them);
-- a level rises by its printed shekels only to within half a shekel —
-- א'8 prints "₪ 1,307" and its levels rise by 1,307.07 — and in eighteen
-- of the nineteen principals' and deputies' tables by no level exactly.
-- The reading adopted: the printed cells govern, and the steps describe
-- them (convention rounding.printed-figure).
`the printed steps do not make the third part's cells` MEANS
        count `all the third part's teachers' step checks` EQUALS 5231
    AND count (`the misses in` `all the third part's teachers' step checks`) EQUALS 1408
    AND all `every level is within half a shekel of its printed shekels` `the third part's principals' and deputies' tables`
    AND all (GIVEN t YIELD null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` (`the grade steps of` t))) `the third part's principals' and deputies' tables`
    AND count (filter (GIVEN t YIELD all (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (c's `agorot off` EQUALS 0)) (`the shekel steps of` t)) `the third part's principals' and deputies' tables`) EQUALS 18
    AND `the cell of` `third-part annex א'8` 2 2 EQUALS JUST 15758.36
    AND `the cell of` `third-part annex א'8` 1 2 EQUALS JUST 14451.29
#ASSERT `the printed steps do not make the third part's cells`

-- (5) Every table rises along its grades and down its rows, so "the grade
-- nearest at or above A" (§46(ב), §71(ב)) is one cell.
#ASSERT all `rises along its grades and down its rows` `all thirty-four third-part tables`
#ASSERT count `all thirty-four third-part tables` EQUALS 34
#ASSERT count `the third part's annexes א'1–א'26` EQUALS 26

-- The tables at work: §46's placement on a conversion row, §35's update.
#ASSERT `the placement in the row` 6300 (`the row labelled` `third-part annex א'3` 2) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 2 6329.98)
#ASSERT `the placement in the row` 21000 (`the row labelled` `third-part annex א'8` 4) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 4 21012.12)
#ASSERT `the third part's table salary on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) `third-part annex א'1` 16 1 EQUALS JUST 7110.28
#ASSERT `the third part's table salary on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2013) `third-part annex א'1` 16 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the cell on` 10400 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) (LIST `the 1.4.2013 table update`) EQUALS 10575
#ASSERT `the cell on` 10400 (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2013) (LIST `the 1.4.2013 table update`) EQUALS 10400
#ASSERT `a reform table cell from 1.4.2013, by the total update` 10000 EQUALS 10575
#ASSERT `the third part's updated tables for` `a supervision or headquarters role` EQUALS `the third part's annexes ב'1–ב'8`
#ASSERT null (`the third part's updated tables for` `the terms off the reform`)

-- The instruments side by side: what this agreement does is what the
-- completion agreement's §92(ב) said it would do, and §5 exhausts a clause
-- §94(ב) of the completion agreement names.
#ASSERT `the third part's cost is allocated from` EQUALS `the January 2013 allocation is made from`
#ASSERT `the third part's tables are updated from` EQUALS `the January 2013 allocation is made from`
#ASSERT `the rate the third part completes` EQUALS `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 April 2013`
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate from 1.4.2013 under the third part` EQUALS `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 April 2013`
#ASSERT `the total update of the reform tables from 1.4.2013` EQUALS `the rate the third part completes`
#ASSERT `the shekel supplements' total update from 1.4.2013` EQUALS `the rate the third part completes`
#ASSERT `the cut of the third part's cost` EQUALS `the cut of the January 2013 allocation`
-- The recitals beside the framework as amended on 11.4.2011: the amendment
-- they name is the one signed that day, and a cut of 0.5% "against the rate
-- of §5.1.3" leaves 5.75% because §5.1.3 completes to 6.25%.
#ASSERT `the framework agreement was amended on` EQUALS `the 2011 amendment was signed on`
#ASSERT `the rate the third part completes` PLUS `the cut of the third part's cost` EQUALS `the allocation 5.1.3 completes to`
#ASSERT elem `the framework clause the third part exhausts` `the framework parts §92 exhausts`
#ASSERT `the third part's recital on section 155(א)`

-- The rest of the agreement at work.
`a teacher off the reform under the third part` MEANS
    `employee` WITH
        `graded on the teaching-staff grade` IS TRUE
        `employed in the State's service`    IS TRUE
        `terms`                              IS `the terms off the reform`

`a reform teacher under the third part` MEANS
    `employee` WITH
        `graded on the teaching-staff grade` IS TRUE
        `employed in the State's service`    IS TRUE
        `terms`                              IS `the reform's terms`

#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under the third part on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) EQUALS 5.75%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under the third part on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2013) EQUALS 4%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under the third part on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2011) EQUALS 2.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement amount under the third part` `a teacher off the reform under the third part` 8000 240 400 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) EQUALS 496.80
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement amount under the third part` `a teacher off the reform under the third part` 8000 240 400 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011) EQUALS 194.40
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement amount under the third part` `a reform teacher under the third part` 8000 240 400 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement under the third part on` (`shekel supplement` TRUE TRUE FALSE 164.06) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) EQUALS 173.493450
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement under the third part on` (`shekel supplement` TRUE TRUE FALSE 164.06) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2013) EQUALS 170.6224
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement under the third part on` (`shekel supplement` TRUE TRUE FALSE 164.06) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011) EQUALS 167.751350
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement under the third part on` (`shekel supplement` TRUE TRUE TRUE 164.06) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013) EQUALS 164.06
#ASSERT `how the third part reaches` `a teacher off the reform under the third part` EQUALS JUST `the 2011 supplement and the shekel supplements updated`
#ASSERT `how the third part reaches` `a reform teacher under the third part` EQUALS JUST `the salary tables updated`
#ASSERT `is an inseparable part of the third part` `an annex`
#ASSERT `a word of the third part reads in another form` masculine feminine FALSE
